<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chippenham</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chippenham is a market town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiltshire">Wiltshire</a>, south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bristol">Bristol</a> Avon. It was a royal estate of the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> kings, and in January 878 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guthrum">Guthrum</a> seized it in a surprise winter attack that drove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> into the marshes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athelney">Athelney</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-edington">Battle of Edington</a> later that year, the Danes surrendered to Alfred at their stronghold, probably Chippenham.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chippenham.jpg" alt="Chippenham" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: My another account (talk) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Andrew%27s_Chippenham.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
